  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no completed experiments, the primary uncertainty is whether a standard multimodal pipeline yields reasonable performance and establishes a useful reference point. config_001 tests a well-motivated multimodal baseline: PCA (n=2000) for RNA, ResNet50 for image, avgpool aggregation, and weighted fusion across multiprofiles. All components are standard and well-established, so the result will be interpretable: if performance is strong, it validates the multimodal hypothesis and gives a ceiling for ablation studies; if weak, it flags which component (encoder, fusion, or profile strategy) is underperforming. Choosing a mid-complexity standard configuration (rather than the simplest unimodal baseline or the most complex transformer/scgpt variant) maximizes information per experiment: it simultaneously provides a multimodal reference, a multiprofile reference, and a weighted-fusion reference, enabling efficient follow-up ablations along any single axis."
}

